      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To find the value of \\(a\\) for which \\(g(a) = 0\\), we start by recalling the definition of the function \\(g(x)\\):\n\n\\[\ng(x) = 3x - 4\n\\]\n\nWe are tasked with solving the equation \\(g(a) = 0\\). This translates to:\n\n\\[\n3a - 4 = 0\n\\]\n\nNext, we solve for \\(a\\):\n\n1. Start from the equation:\n   \\[\n   3a - 4 = 0\n   \\]\n\n2. Add \\(4\\) to both sides to isolate the term with \\(a\\):\n   \\[\n   3a - 4 + 4 = 0 + 4\n   \\]\n   Simplifying this gives:\n   \\[\n   3a = 4\n   \\]\n\n3. Divide both sides by \\(3\\) to solve for \\(a\\):\n   \\[\n   a = \\frac{4}{3}\n   \\]\n\nHence, the value of \\(a\\) such that \\(g(a) = 0\\) is \\(\\boxed{\\frac{4}{3}}\\).",
